    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (per-city sequence).\n\n**`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 `nextCustomerCode` now takes the city as well:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- `NNNN` = per-city 4-digit zero-padded sequence (one more than owners already in that city, counted case-insensitively via a new `countOwnersInCity` helper), replacing the old global `findAll().size() + 1`.\n\n**Values derived from `customerCode`** \u2014 `Owner.getMembershipNumber()` is `customerCode + \"-M<YY>\"`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`). I updated its javadoc example accordingly.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated `openapi.yml` descriptions and examples for `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` to reflect the new format.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserts `customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
