    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic:\n\n- `nextCustomerCode` cleanly gained a `city` parameter and composes the three parts (`city3`, `last3`, sequence) with the same `String.format` approach it already used.\n- The new `countOwnersInCity` helper is a direct structural sibling of the existing `countNamesakes` \u2014 same `private static int`, same `findAll()` iteration, same case-insensitive comparison, same javadoc style. A maintainer would find it entirely natural sitting next to it, and the per-attribute counting pattern was already established here, so this isn't a new/duplicated idiom.\n- Logic lives in the right unit: `BuildOwner` is where derived creation-time fields are computed.\n- The membership number is correctly left to derive automatically from `customerCode` (`getMembershipNumber()` concatenates `customerCode`), so only the javadoc example needed the `LON-` prefix \u2014 no redundant logic was introduced, which is the right call per the spec.\n- OpenAPI description/example and the `Owner` javadoc example were both updated to match, keeping docs in sync.\n\nNo catch-all growth, no misplaced logic, no unnecessary duplication.",
